- Bilung Lee attended a seminar on Stateflow, a new product of the
  MathWorks, Inc. who owns MATLAB, Simulink and Real-Time Workshop.

  Stateflow is based on the Statecharts formalism. The graphical editor
  of Stateflow allows users to draw the FSM by state transition
  diagram. Moreover, FSMs can be hierarchical or parallel combinations
  in the similar way as in Statecharts. The conditions (guards) are
  Boolean expressions, and the actions associated with a transition can
  be a function call, an event to be broadcast, or a variable to be
  assigned a value. Stateflow also has the option of initial entry or
  history entry for a hierarchical state. However, they don't have the
  option of preemptive or non-preemptive transitions. Stateflow keeps
  non-compositional constructs, like inter-level transitions and state
  reference, as in Statecharts. A new added graphical syntax is called
  "Junction". A "Junction" provides a decision point in the FSM, where
  one of several transition can be followed. This achieves the same
  effect as allowing more than one transition to be executed in one
  reaction. For example,

                        t2
        t1          |--------> State
State -----> Junction 
                    |--------> State
                        t3    

  Thus, "t1 and t2" or "t1 and t3" will be executed in one reaction. 
  In addition to the graphical editor, Stateflow has other build-in tools:
      - Explorer: Browse, define and modify non-graphical objects in
        Stateflow diagram.
      - Finder: Search a list of objects.
      - Debugger: Debug and animate the Stateflow diagram.

  Stateflow has been integrated with Simulink, i.e. a Stateflow diagram
  can be used as a module inside the Simulink. Simulink is a block
  diagram environment for modeling and simulating a system.

  The Stateflow Coder allows users to generate C code for a particular
  target processor. Code generated by Stateflow Coder can be
  incorporated into code generated by Real-Time Workshop which is the
  code generation machine for Simulink.

